  <section class="article-head"><h1>Disclaimer</h1></section>
  <div class="prose">
<p><em>Last updated: October 16, 2026 — 11:53 PM (Pakistan time)</em></p>
    <p>This Disclaimer explains the limits of the information published on Talha M Blog (talhablog.com). Please read it together with our <a href="/terms/">Terms of Use</a> and our <a href="/privacy/">Privacy Policy</a>. By using this website, you acknowledge this Disclaimer.</p>

    <h2>General information only</h2>
    <p>Everything published on Talha M Blog — news explanations, background articles, life stories, lists, guides and summaries — is provided for general information and education only. Nothing on this website is professional advice, an official statement, or a substitute for original documents and the authorities involved in a story.</p>

    <h2>Not professional advice</h2>
    <p>Talha M Blog does not provide legal, medical, financial, investment or other professional advice. Some stories mention health, medicines, money, business, law or court cases, because those subjects appear in the news; reporting on them is not a recommendation. For decisions about your health, your money, your legal situation or your safety, please consult a qualified professional or an official authority in your country who can consider your own circumstances. Acting only on a simplified news explanation would be unwise.</p>

    <h2>Accuracy, completeness and developing stories</h2>
    <p>We check facts against reliable sources before publishing, and for important stories we compare reports from at least three independent sources. Even with this care, news can change: eyewitness accounts may differ, official figures may be revised, charges may be amended, and early reports may turn out to be incomplete. We cannot guarantee that every article is perfectly accurate, complete and current at the exact moment you read it. Where reports conflict, or a claim rests on unnamed sources, we say so inside the story. When we discover an error — or a reader reports one that checks out — we correct the article and show an "Updated" date. If you believe something on this website is wrong, please tell us through our <a href="/contact/">Contact page</a>; corrections help every future reader.</p>

    <h2>Allegations, court cases and right of reply</h2>
    <p>Some stories cover crimes, arrests, trials and disputes. When we write that a person was arrested, charged or accused, we are reporting what officials, courts or other sources have said — we are not declaring that the person did what they are accused of. Charges and claims are allegations unless and until a court decides otherwise, and every person is presumed innocent until proven guilty. If you, or an organisation you represent, are mentioned in a story and you believe something in it is wrong or unfair, email us at contact@talhablog.com with the story link and your response. We will check it promptly and, where it is fair, correct the story or add your response.</p>

    <h2>Sources</h2>
    <p>Our stories are based on reports from news agencies, newspapers, official statements and other sources, which we name at the end of each story, with links to the original reports so that readers can check them directly. Naming or linking a source does not mean we agree with everything that source publishes, and a source report can itself later be corrected by its publisher.</p>

    <h2>Views and neutrality</h2>
    <p>Reporting about a person, a company, a party, a government or an event does not mean that Talha M Blog supports or opposes them. Quotations and claims belong to the people and organisations that made them; we report them to explain a story, not to endorse every claim. Our aim is explanation, not campaigning.</p>

    <h2>Reader comments</h2>
    <p>Comments under our stories are written by readers, and they express the views of the people who post them — not the views of Talha M Blog. Comments appear immediately, so we cannot check each one before it appears. We may hide or remove comments that break the rules in our <a href="/terms/">Terms of Use</a>. If you see a comment that is abusive, false or unlawful, email us with the story link and we will review it.</p>

    <h2>How our stories are prepared</h2>
    <p>Every story we publish is based on research from reliable sources and written in our own words. We carefully review the information, verify facts, and edit each article before publication to ensure accuracy and quality. Our editor takes full responsibility for the content published on this website. We are committed to providing trustworthy information and never knowingly publishing fabricated quotes, misleading statistics, or false events.</p>

    <h2>Images are illustrations</h2>
    <p>The pictures published with our stories are illustrations made for Talha M Blog to represent the subject of the story. They are not real press photographs, and they should not be treated as visual proof of a person, a place or an event. In the rare case that a real photograph from another source is ever used, it will be credited on the page.</p>

    <h2>External links</h2>
    <p>Our articles link to outside websites for original reports, official statements and further reading. We do not control those websites; they may change or disappear, and their content is their owners' responsibility. A link is provided for information, and it is not a guarantee that everything on the linked website is accurate, safe or suitable for you.</p>

    <h2>Products, prices and tools</h2>
    <p>Stories may mention products, phones, apps, prices or services because they are part of the news. Prices and offers can change quickly and can vary by country and by seller. Mentioning a product is not a promise about its price or quality, and it is not personalised advice to buy or to avoid something. Please check the current details with the seller or provider before making a decision.</p>

    <h2>Advertising</h2>
    <p>This website has applied to display advertising served by Google AdSense, and advertisements will appear once our application is approved. Our application is currently under review, Auto ads is switched on, and no advertisements are shown yet. When advertisements appear, they will be selected automatically by Google's systems. The appearance of an advertisement on Talha M Blog does not mean that we have tested, verified or endorsed the advertised product, service or company. Any purchase or agreement you make with an advertiser is entirely between you and them. Our <a href="/privacy/">Privacy Policy</a> explains how advertising cookies and consent choices will work.</p>

    <h2>Use at your own judgement</h2>
    <p>We work hard to be accurate and fair, and we correct our mistakes openly — but readers should always weigh important information against official and primary sources before acting on it. To the extent allowed by law, Talha M Blog accepts no responsibility for decisions taken, or losses suffered, based on information read on this website.</p>

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>If you have any question about this Disclaimer, or you want to report a mistake, please email us at <a href="mailto:contact@talhablog.com">contact@talhablog.com</a> or use our <a href="/contact/">Contact page</a>. We will do our best to answer clearly and honestly.</p>

